<p>In the latest turn in the Israel-Iran war, strikes reached core Gulf energy infrastructure on March 19 after Israel hit Iran’s South Pars gas field and Iran retaliated against Qatar’s Ras Laffan gas facilities, sending oil and gas prices sharply higher. South Pars is Iran’s main gas field and part of the larger South Pars/North Dome reserve it shares with Qatar, which makes this exchange especially significant for regional energy supplies and global LNG markets. President Trump said Israel acted alone in striking South Pars and said the United States and Qatar were not involved. He also warned that the U.S. would &quot;massively blow up&quot; the field if Iran attacked Qatar again. Later reporting said Israeli officials told Reuters that Washington had been informed or was involved, underscoring conflicting accounts about U.S. prior knowledge even as Trump also said Israel would not carry out further attacks on South Pars. The escalation matters far beyond the battlefield because it puts some of the world’s most important gas export infrastructure at risk and raises fears of a wider regional confrontation. Even so, Trump’s message that Israel would not strike South Pars again unless Iran hit Qatar again offered at least a narrow opening for de-escalation after a day of rapid escalation.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/42yCHZlyeOuc2DVw14c1exXuFdKlB24QHkdccV_N72zesP0ztBV9kDlKQvrc1ikB-Za2ysdnxKknPcOx6nvdPbxob3ekOhnBrtCnrc4iFZRqXoUYPR7Gfq41DpSQaSgFaqfbb_DZciwbG7ojdvTj32StGSAyiq0_70J6COy_C_1c7z_WaTW8XKuxF-od-9SO4wW5cRCeld816pJjr2iVgBuTyQYqD6xwhJBtXr4e0KSEWeQd09Lz' alt='A fire near the South Pars gas field, in Bushehr Province, Iran, on March 18, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Shared reserve: The South Pars/North Dome field spans nearly 10,000 square kilometers and holds an estimated 1,800 trillion cubic feet of gas, making it the world’s largest natural gas field.</li><li>Domestic reliance: South Pars provides about 70% of Iran’s domestic natural gas output, so damage there directly threatens Iranian power generation, industry, and exports.</li><li>Regional spread: Beyond Qatar, multiple reports said Iranian strikes or threats reached energy sites in Kuwait, the UAE, and Saudi Arabia, widening concern that the conflict could pull in more Gulf states.</li><li>Iraq disruption: A senior Iraqi official told Reuters that Iranian gas flows to Iraq stopped as Tehran diverted supply for domestic use after the South Pars strike, affecting a country that gets roughly one-third to 40% of its gas and power needs from Iran.</li></ul><blockquote>NO MORE ATTACKS WILL BE MADE BY ISRAEL - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: Trump said Israel acted alone in the South Pars strike, insisted the U.S. and Qatar were not involved, and paired that denial with a threat of direct U.S. retaliation if Iran attacked Qatar again. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/19/world/middleeast/trump-iran-south-pars-gas-field.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Israeli officials: Israeli officials cited by Reuters said Washington knew about or helped coordinate the South Pars attack, directly challenging Trump’s initial public account. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/mar/19/iran-war-live-updates-oil-prices-gas-field-strikes-pentagon-more-funds-trump-news'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Qatar: Qatar condemned both the Israeli strike on South Pars and the Iranian attack on Ras Laffan, casting itself as an uninvolved state whose energy infrastructure had been pulled into the conflict. (<a href='https://theweek.com/world-news/recriminations-iran-war-gas-fields'>The Week</a>)</li><li>Iran: Iranian officials and the Revolutionary Guards framed attacks on Gulf energy sites as retaliation and warned neighboring states that their facilities could become targets if U.S.-Israeli attacks continued. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-tehran-vows-zero-restraint-if-energy-sites-hit/live-76422645'>DW</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/iran-war-israel-strike-south-pars-gas-field-trump-threat-oil-gas-prices/'>War escalates, energy prices spike after Israeli strike on Iran gas field</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/3/19/why-are-irans-south-pars-gasfield-qatars-ras-laffan-so-significant'>Why are Iran’s South Pars gasfield, Qatar’s Ras Laffan, so significant?</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/19/attacks-on-gulf-energy-facilities-intensify-fueling-fears-of-a-gas-war_6751601_4.html'>Attacks on Gulf energy facilities intensify, fueling fears of a &#x27;gas war&#x27;</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://novaramedia.com/2026/03/19/trump-threatens-to-blow-up-the-worlds-largest-gasfield/'>Trump Threatens to ‘Blow Up’ the World’s Largest Gasfield</a> - novaramedia.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/635540-israel-iran-chain-reaction/'>Israel has just set off a chain reaction that will set the Gulf on fire</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/video-tehran-intensifies-attacks-on-gulf-energy-facilities-after-israel-hits/'>Tehran intensifies attacks on Gulf energy facilities after Israel hits Iranian gas field</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/03/19/trump-threatens-to-entirely-blow-up-irans-largest-gas-field-if-it-attacks-qatars-lng-again'>Trump threatens to &#x27;entirely blow up&#x27; Iran&#x27;s largest gas field if it attacks Qatar&#x27;s LNG again</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1983590/israeli-attack-on-largest-gas-field-turns-middle-east-into-powder-keg'>Israeli attack on largest gas field turns Middle East into powder keg</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-tehran-vows-zero-restraint-if-energy-sites-hit/live-76422645'>Iran war: Tehran vows &#x27;zero restraint&#x27; i